# filters.txt conventions

- Each site gets its own section headed by a comment: `# Block ads for https://www.example.no`
- Put new filters under the site's existing section; add a new section at the end of the file only if the site has none.
- Separate sections with one blank line.
- Use sub-comments inside a section to explain non-obvious filters (e.g. `# Block betting ads`, `# Home page`).
- Use the hostname style already used in that section. For new sites, prefer the bare domain (`finn.no##`) so subdomains are covered.
- Comments use `#`; the `!` lines at the top are the list header — do not change them.
- Do not add duplicates; check whether an existing filter already covers the element.

```
# Block ads for https://www.example.no
example.no##advt-component
example.no##[id^="adPlacement"]
# Sponsored articles
example.no##article:has(.sponsored-label)
```
